<title>CYPRUS: MEES SEES IRAQ EXPORTING 25-30 MLN BLS TO SEPT 5.</title>
<headline>MEES SEES IRAQ EXPORTING 25-30 MLN BLS TO SEPT 5.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq plans to export about 25-30 million barrels of oil in what remains of a 90-day period to September 5 under the second phase of the U.N's oil-for-food scheme, the Middle East Economic Survey (MEES) said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;At a price of about $16/barrel, this would leave a shortfall of some 40 million barrels -- or over $600 million in value terms -- below the monetary target of $1.07 billion for the 90 days,&quot; the Cyprus-based newsletter reported.</p>
<p>&quot;If a sufficient number of signed contracts are delivered to the U.N. overseers early this week -- say Monday morning -- this could possibly allow exports to begin before the end of the week -- say August 15. This would leave some 22 days for exporting before the gate closes on September 5, and the second 90-day period starts,&quot; MEES said.</p>
</text>
